 - `ui.List` row selection paints the accent color itself (`Selected()`). The browser covers it with an opaque `selectionFill`.
 - Dialogs focus their first focusable element. A focused button keeps Enter, so main buttons use `AutoFocus` (only in dialogs without a text field).
 - Names are renamed in place (`app/rename.go`), not with `ui.EditableText`: in a `List` it takes the row a click chooses for one chosen before the click, so a plain click on a row starts editing it half a second later. Asking a row's text `Clicked()` (or `Pressed`/`DoubleClicked`) makes it the click's target and the list stops choosing the row; `HandleInput` returning false watches presses without taking them.
-- There is no new-folder button or dialog: the maker (`app/newfolder.go`), an accent row after the list's files (a `Header` row, so it is never chosen) or the grid's last tile (`makerID`), makes folders and picks uploads, and lights up while files are dragged over the window (`listing.over`, which scrolls it into view). A new folder is named in a draft row at the top (`draftID`, put back each frame by `placeDraft`); a click away with its name untouched gives up. Cmd-Shift-N starts it.
+- The folder's actions live in a toolbar on the path bar (`app/browser.go`'s `filesToolbar`): a new folder (`folder-plus`), the sort menu, the view switch, the clipboard-link button, refresh, and the upload pill at the end; the folder's own name and search sit before them, and a button's box is where a folder made from it flies from (`listing.makerAt`). The maker (`app/newfolder.go`) is no longer a place for buttons: the grid's last tile is a whole "新建" tile that makes a folder on a click (a plus, or an upload while files are dragged over the window, `listing.over`), and the list's maker row is only the drop hint, in the accent color saying where dropped files will go, built only while files are dragged so it takes no room at the foot of a full folder. An empty folder says "这里还空着" and offers one upload of its own, labelled apart from the toolbar's. A new folder is named in a draft row at the top (`draftID`, put back each frame by `placeDraft`); a click away with its name untouched gives up. Cmd-Shift-N starts it from the toolbar's button box.
 - Things coming into a folder fly in (`app/landing.go`): rows glide to make room (`glideRow`, the listing holding the glide: `AnimateTo`/`Jump` on a list row take its name's clicks), then a card over the page (`flight`) goes from where the thing was put (drop point, button, draft row) to the row, which stays hidden until it lands. A `Transition` `Match` cannot do it: a list clips its rows to their slots, so a row coming from elsewhere shows only once it is there. A row the list chooses paints the accent under itself even while hidden, so the folder made is chosen once it lands (`chooseLanded`).
 - Virtualized `List` rows get no enter/exit transitions. Staggered entrances use `Keyframes` inside the row (`entering` in `browser.go`).
 - The grid view is not `ui.GridView`: GridView builds each line as an element, so a tile that a resize moves to another line is built anew and jumps. `app/grid.go` positions tiles itself, all under one parent keyed by fsid (percent `Left`/`Width`, so the width never lags), and on a cell change `Jump`s the slot's offset to where it showed and `AnimateTo`s it back to 0. Element `Transition`s don't help here: MyGo skips layout transitions on frames where the window resized.
